      "score": 78,
      "comments": 37,
      "author": "mtlynch",
      "published": "2026-10-07T13:09:33Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Regurgitating official documentation or AI boilerplate without real-world production context, edge cases, or benchmark data alienates senior engineering readers.",
        "Publishing incomplete code snippets without reproducible runtime environments, explicit dependencies, or error-handling paths drastically reduces a tutorial's utility.",
        "Advocating complex distributed architectures like microservices or Kubernetes for simple workloads promotes premature optimization and harmful architectural cargo-culting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "Calling a function in C without naming it",
      "url": "https://wiro.world/posts/calling-c-func-without-naming-it/",
