      "score": 25,
      "comments": 3,
      "author": "mrnossiom",
      "published": "2026-10-07T18:15:02Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Dynamic resolution via function pointers, base address offsets, or dlsym/GetProcAddress bypasses static import table and symbol analysis.",
        "Malware leverages anonymous indirect calls and computed jumps to evade EDR API hooking and static signature detection.",
        "Enforce compiler-level Control Flow Integrity (CFI) and memory protections like W^X to detect and block illicit indirect execution."
      ]
